---
import Icon from "./Icon.astro"
import ActivityConsole from "./ActivityConsole.astro"
import RemoteSetup from "./RemoteSetup.astro"
---
<section id="controls" class="system-section" aria-labelledby="controls-title">
  <h2 id="controls-title" class="sr-only">Recovery and services</h2>
  <div class="section-heading">
    <div><p>Recovery runs independently of this page.</p></div>
    <div class="heading-actions">
      <button class="button" id="open-desktop" type="button" aria-describedby="desktop-status" disabled><Icon name="desktop" size={16} />Open OpenCode Desktop</button>
      <button class="button" id="recover-all" type="button" disabled>Recover All</button>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p id="desktop-status" class="control-detail" role="status">Checking the local Desktop launcher…</p>
  <RemoteSetup />
  <ActivityConsole />
  <div class="control-overview">
    <article class="panel control-panel">
      <div class="control-heading"><h3>PC → VPS connection</h3><span id="control-connection" class="status-pill neutral">Checking…</span></div>
      <p id="recovery-status" role="status">Connecting to the independent local supervisor…</p>
      <p id="network-detail" class="control-detail" role="status">Internet and VPS reachability are checked separately.</p>
      <p id="recovery-detail" class="control-detail"></p>
      <div class="control-settings">
        <label><input id="auto-reconnect" name="auto-reconnect" type="checkbox" disabled /> Automatic reconnect</label>
        <label id="auto-wake-setting" hidden><input id="auto-wake" name="auto-wake" type="checkbox" disabled /> Automatic remote-host wake</label>
      </div>
      <div class="control-wake">
        <span id="remote-state">Remote host state unknown</span>
        <div class="remote-actions">
          <button id="wake-remote" class="button" type="button" disabled hidden>Wake Remote Host</button>
          <button id="stop-remote" class="button button-danger" type="button" disabled hidden>Stop Remote Host…</button>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p id="remote-power-notice" class="control-detail" hidden>Wake may resume compute billing. Availability depends on the provider.</p>
      <p class="control-detail">Stopping interrupts active requests and disables automatic reconnect and wake. Saved files and relay state are preserved.</p>
    </article>
    <article class="panel control-panel">
      <div class="control-heading"><h3>ChatGPT sign-in</h3><span id="auth-state" class="status-pill neutral">Checking…</span></div>
      <p id="auth-countdown" class="auth-countdown">—</p>
      <p id="auth-deadline" class="control-detail">Reading local authentication metadata…</p>
      <p class="control-detail">This is the access token’s expiry, not a usage-limit reset. OpenCode may refresh it automatically.</p>
      <p class="control-detail">If sign-in is required, use OpenCode’s Connect provider flow. This page never refreshes tokens or makes model requests.</p>
    </article>
  </div>
  <div id="control-notice" class="notice" role="status" hidden></div>
  <article class="panel service-panel">
    <div class="control-heading"><h3>Services</h3><button id="restart-all" class="text-button" type="button" disabled>Restart All…</button></div>
    <div id="service-controls" class="service-controls"><p class="control-detail">Service controls are available even when the local gateway is down.</p></div>
    <p class="control-detail">Restart preserves tokens, sessions, cached chunks, and saved responses. Active requests may be interrupted.</p>
  </article>
</section>
